[11:09:35] [INFO] ================================================================================
[11:09:35] [INFO] EXCELLENT AGREEMENT: TEP scaling relation consistent with observation.
[11:09:35] [INFO] ================================================================================
[11:09:35] [INFO] 
[11:09:35] [INFO] INTERPRETATION:
[11:09:35] [INFO] ===============
[11:09:35] [INFO] The TEP scaling relation Γ_TEP = 2Γ_N - 1 gives 0.50:
[11:09:35] [INFO] 
[11:09:35] [INFO] 1. Uses measured Newtonian slope Γ_N = 0.7476777251184834 (from CMC simulations)
[11:09:35] [INFO] 2. Applies the TEP framework's scaling assumption: potential vs acceleration
[11:09:35] [INFO] 3. Result: Γ_TEP = 2Γ_N - 1 = 0.50
[11:09:35] [INFO] 
[11:09:35] [INFO] This is consistent with the observed Γ = 0.393 ± 0.078
[11:09:35] [INFO] at 0.9σ. The agreement confirms that the TEP framework's scaling
[11:09:35] [INFO] assumption (potential-dominated vs acceleration-dominated) is compatible
[11:09:35] [INFO] with the data. It is a consistency check, not an independent prediction,
[11:09:35] [INFO] because the relation depends on the TEP formalism's premise.
